# Partial-catch guard, the other direction (error-model.md §11 Increment 2 (C)):
# catching ONLY Fault.Overflow does NOT swallow a div-by-zero. Here `10 / 0` is
# a DivByZero, UNCAUGHT by the Overflow pattern, so it PANICS `division by zero`
# — uniformly on both backends.
void main():
    int z = 0
    int r = (10 / z) catch Fault.Overflow: 0
    print(f"{r}")
